# Pin line endings so a diff means something.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (2026-08-12)
# This repo was 18 files CRLF / 66 LF while its upstream sibling
# (LiteSuite/packages/liteharness) was uniformly LF. A 3-way merge between the two
# reported SIX modules as 100% conflict — every line "changed" — because the line
# endings differed, not the code. Normalised, the real conflict surface was 22 hunks
# in 4 files, and two of the six merged clean.
#
# That difference is not cosmetic. It is why a ~1,700-line divergence between two live
# trees stayed invisible for ten weeks: nobody could read a diff that was always
# entirely red. An unreadable diff is a diff nobody reads.
#
# A related trap already cost a session: a "337-byte repo-vs-cache delta" was chased as
# drift when it was only CRLF.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.py   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf

# Windows-only launchers must keep CRLF or cmd.exe mis-parses them.
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf

*.whl  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.db   binary
